WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.010
In 1990, foreign direct investment into
Vietnam was 0.18 billion US dollars.

2
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:11.230
In 2025, it was 22.0 billion.

3
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:17.210
On ILO estimates, 64 per cent of
Vietnam's workers were in farming in 2000.

4
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.270
By 2024, 26 per cent.

5
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.470
Samsung Electronics, a
South Korean company,

6
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.650
runs factories in Bac Ninh, Thai
Nguyen and Ho Chi Minh City.

7
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.130
They make mobile devices
and consumer electronics.

8
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.250
So who gains from these factories,
and who carries the risk?

9
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.230
In this mission, you'll
trace how Vietnam's trade,

10
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.590
jobs and incomes changed as it globalised.

11
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.690
Then you'll sort Samsung's
impacts: economic,

12
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.590
social and environmental,
positive and negative.

13
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.610
Your mission: decide who gains from
Samsung's factories in Vietnam,

14
00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.600
and who carries the risk.
